&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Via is on a mission to create public transportation systems that provide greater access to jobs, healthcare, and education. Our platform serves as the technology backbone for modern transit networks, transforming antiquated and siloed public transportation systems into smart, data-driven, and efficient digital networks. With hundreds of agency partners around the world, Via is recognized as the leading transportation technology and service provider globally.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an &lt;strong&gt;Administrative Specialist &lt;/strong&gt;at Via, you will serve as the central hub connecting transit technology, drivers, and riders across Fixed Route, Paratransit, and Microtransit operations. This role delivers high-quality customer assistance, manages real-time dispatch and trip scheduling, processes rider eligibility applications, and maintains accurate administrative, fare, and operational records.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role will be in-person 5 days a week&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer Care and Administration:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary, welcoming point of contact for walk-in visitors and callers, assisting with route and schedule planning, issuing employee/passenger ID badges, selling passes, and managing daily cash register transactions, reconciliations, and group billing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee driver sign-in/sign-out processes, audit post-trip manifests, reconcile collected fares, and accurately log daily mileage and trip data into core operating systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process Paratransit Eligibility:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Receive, review, and process ADA Paratransit and Mobility eligibility applications, verify documentation, update rider accessibility profiles, and track eligibility expiration dates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Schedule, Dispatch, &amp;amp; Monitor Live Service:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create manifests for Paratransit and Microtransit services, and adjust schedules as needed to manage daily operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain radio communication with drivers, direct and monitor bus activity across the system, provide real-time updates on passenger pick-ups/drop-offs, and triage live operational issues to ensure safe, reliable, and on-time service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrive in fast-paced environments: able to make sound decisions on the fly, oversee multiple tasks simultaneously, and prioritize effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tech savvy, able to learn new software and adapt to changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An empathetic and effective communicator who finds the right tone in any context and genuinely enjoys supporting people in person or over the phone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Calm under pressure and able to think on your feet&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to learn and a commitment to great service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive, Observant, and keen to improve: if something’s not working, you come up with a better way while being able to anticipate and prevent problems before they start&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An exceptional team player: people love working with you, and you can quickly contribute to cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership mentality: take full responsibility for delivering great service to customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible and adaptable across different shifts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salary Range: $20.48/HR, with routine increases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Benefits options available for Full-Time employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There has never been a more exciting time to be on the cutting edge of public mobility. Ready to join the ride?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Via is an equal opportunity employer.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Via is using technology to transform transportation around the world. From changing a single person’s daily commute to reducing humanity’s collective environmental footprint - we’ve got huge goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an &lt;strong&gt;Algorithm&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Developer &lt;/strong&gt;at Via, you’ll join our R&amp;amp;D center in London, as part of the Core R&amp;amp;D group, which is responsible for developing and maintaining Via’s proprietary algorithms and the services that run them in production. The position requires deep knowledge of algorithms, data structures, software engineering methodologies and best practices. You will maintain and improve current algorithms and business logic, as well as develop new technical products and systems that support the various needs we have here at Via. If you’re a developer by heart and enjoy working on large-scale algorithms in a hands-on environment, this position might be just for you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take full ownership of large and complex code base that implements Via’s core algorithm&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain multiple mission critical services&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Immediate impact to Via’s thousands of daily passengers and clients around the world, like making our booking application respond to users significantly faster.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work in close collaboration with devops teams and algorithms developers and researchers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;M.Sc. in Computer Science / Software Engineering / Mathematics / similar field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Minimum of 3 years of hands-on industry experience in backend development (Python)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Experience with DevOps in cloud infrastructure (Kubernetes, etc.) — strong advantage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-stringify-indent=&quot;0&quot; data-stringify-border=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Experience in architecture and maintaining cloud systems — strong advantage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a solid background in software engineering methodologies, such as git, CI/CD&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fast learner: you can quickly master concepts, disciplines and methods&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team player: you work well with people, as well as by yourself&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pragmatic: you know how to deconstruct a problem into few smaller problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Concise: you get stuff done, in a simple, elegant way.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation and Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Joining a global employer with over 700 mobility deployments in 50+ countries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Becoming part of a company that was awarded for its commitment to social good&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation including equity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A hybrid working model and a spacious office near Chancery Lane, where you can enjoy weekly team lunches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive health scheme offered through AXA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partnership with YellowNest, a salary exchange benefit that helps reduce childcare fees for working parents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re Via, and we build technology that changes the way the world moves. We’re driven by a simple mission: to create modern and efficient public transportation systems that provide far greater access to jobs, healthcare, and education. With our best in class suite of products, we make transit thrive.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our teams of worldclass engineers, data-scientists, product managers, operations specialists, marketers, transit experts and more bring cutting-edge AI-powered software and innovative technology-enabled operations to our partners across the globe. Founded in 2012, Via builds solutions to digitize, automate, and enable data-driven decision making for entire transportation networks; fixed-route buses, microtransit, paratransit, school buses, autonomous vehicles, and more.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re excited to be at the forefront of modernizing the future of transportation, are up for solving tough problems, and willing to become/already are a transit nerd, we are the place for you. Even if your past experience doesn’t align perfectly with every qualification in the job description for this role, we encourage you to apply. You may be just the right candidate for this or other opportunities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ready to join the ride?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Via is an equal opportunity employer.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Via is using technology to transform transportation around the world. From changing a single person’s daily commute to reducing humanity’s collective environmental footprint - we’ve got huge goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Algorithm&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Researcher &lt;/strong&gt;at Via, you’ll join our R&amp;amp;D center in London, as part of the Core R&amp;amp;D group, which is responsible for developing and maintaining Via’s proprietary algorithms and the services that run them in production. The role sits at the intersection of algorithm development, data science, and software engineering. You’ll work on complex algorithmic problems, explore and evaluate different approaches, and turn your solutions into reliable production systems that support Via’s transportation networks around the world. If you enjoy combining analytical thinking, algorithms, data, and hands-on development, this position might be just for you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, develop, and improve Via’s core algorithms and business logic, solving complex real-world problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explore and evaluate algorithmic approaches using data, experimentation, and analytical methods.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain mission-critical services that bring algorithmic solutions into production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with large datasets to analyze system behavior and improve the performance of our algorithms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership of complex technical problems, from initial research and exploration through to production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work in close collaboration with algorithm developers, researchers, data scientists, and software engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;M.Sc. or Ph.D. in Computer Science / Mathematics / Statistics / Operations Research / similar quantitative field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of relevant industry experience in algorithm development, data science, research, or software engineering with a strong algorithmic focus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of algorithms, data structures, and analytical problem-solving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Python skills and experience developing production-quality code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with data and applying data science, optimization, or analytical techniques to solve complex problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience taking algorithms, models, or prototypes and turning them into production systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with DevOps and cloud infrastructure (Kubernetes, etc.) — strong advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in architecture and maintaining cloud systems — strong advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curious and analytical: you enjoy exploring different approaches and understanding the data behind your solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pragmatic: you can break complex problems into smaller problems and find simple, effective solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on: you enjoy taking ideas from research or experimentation all the way into production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation and Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Becoming part of a company that was awarded for its commitment to social good:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are one of 17 Ventures That Embody the U.N.’s 17 Sustainable Development Goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inc. Magazine’s “Best in Business” Awardee in the software category for Companies That Put Purpose Before Profit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation including equity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A spacious office near Chancery Lane, where you can enjoy weekly team lunches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive health scheme offered through AXA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partnership with YellowNest, a salary exchange benefit that helps reduce childcare fees for working parents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cycle to Work Scheme - multiple options via Green Commute Initiative (GCI)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There has never been a more exciting time to be on the cutting edge of public mobility. Ready to join the ride?&lt;/p&gt;
