&lt;p&gt;Via is using technology to transform transportation around the world. From changing a single person’s daily commute to reducing humanity’s collective environmental footprint — we’ve got huge goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Business Operations Specialist&lt;/strong&gt; at Via, you&#39;ll run the invoicing, payment, and contracting work that keeps our business operations moving. You&#39;ll be part of a global company that is a world leader in transit technology, working with an international team on our mission to build better public transportation systems. At the same time, you&#39;ll join a smaller team in Tokyo, in a region where Via is growing rapidly, so your work has real visibility and plenty of room for you to grow with it. It&#39;s a fast-paced environment that values ownership, moving fast, and solving meaningful problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the invoice and payment process from start to finish: prepare and process invoices, PO requests, and payment documentation, and track down missing information so nothing stalls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive contracting from first request to final signature: collect vendor details, prepare agreements, arrange signatures, and keep our contract logs accurate and up to date.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain the trackers and filing systems the team uses to see where everything stands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the go-to contact for internal teams and external partners, keeping communication fast, clear, and easy to follow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take part in legal document check-ins with our colleagues across the globe several times a month.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep day-to-day operations running smoothly, including scheduling and general administrative workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pick up ad-hoc coordination tasks as they come up: spot the next step, gather what’s needed, and move it forward without waiting for instructions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 10 years of experience in operations, finance admin, invoicing, or coordination, ideally including managing commercial contracts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Native-level or bilingual &lt;strong&gt;Japanese&lt;/strong&gt;, written and spoken.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business-level &lt;strong&gt;English&lt;/strong&gt; or higher, written and spoken. English is our company language, and you’ll work with international teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tech-savvy with hands-on experience in Google Workspace, Slack, Salesforce, or AI tools—or a proven track record of getting up to speed on new platforms fast.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong administrative skills and attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A “get things done” mindset: you take initiative, respond quickly, and work independently with little supervision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resourceful and flexible, and happy to work in a fast-paced environment where priorities change and the job description isn’t always clear-cut.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working Conditions:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hourly rate of ¥2,500–3,000&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ll start as a contractor for one year, with the potential to convert to full-time based on mutual discussion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Core hours are 09:30–17:30, five days a week, for roughly 30–40 hours per week. Quarter-end periods require overtime work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid: one day a week in our Toranomon, Tokyo office, and remote the rest of the week.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Weekly legal document check-in meetings aligned with European time zones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health insurance covered by the company, with a company top-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commuting costs covered for commutes within 90 minutes of our Tokyo office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There has never been a more exciting time to be on the cutting edge of public mobility.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
