&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Customer Service Representative&lt;/strong&gt;, TCRTA&amp;nbsp;at Via, you will be the human connection between our technology and the people who depend on it -helping hundreds of thousands of riders and drivers across hundreds of cities every day. You&#39;ll keep our on-demand services running smoothly, sitting at the heart of our Operations team and gaining hands-on experience across operations, technology management, and on-demand mobility in a fast-moving, mission-driven environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively manage daily operations, adapting to real-time input from drivers, riders, and the Operations team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Schedule and book rides for passengers,&amp;nbsp; delivering smooth and efficient customer experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide prompt, supportive assistance to drivers and passengers, by responding to questions or concerns with telephone and email support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively triage live operational issues and take action to prioritize customer satisfaction and ensure that any issues are resolved.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage knowledge of Via products and services to make ad hoc decisions with little guidance acting as the final decision-maker for escalated live support issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow with your tasks and responsibilities, if you so choose, and increase your compensation accordingly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrive in fast-paced environments: able to make sound decisions on the fly, oversee multiple tasks simultaneously, and prioritize effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tech savvy, able to learn new software and adapt to changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An empathetic and effective communicator who finds the right tone in any context and genuinely enjoys supporting people over the phone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Calm under pressure and able to think on your feet — no prior call center experience required; what matters is a willingness to learn and a commitment to great service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive, Observant, and keen to improve: if something’s not working, you come up with a better way while being able to anticipate and prevent problems before they start&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An exceptional team player: people love working with you, and you can quickly contribute to cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership mentality: take full responsibility for delivering great service to customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible and adaptable across different shifts; while we try to accommodate individual schedules, this role requires some availability outside standard hours to support our 24/7 operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Successful completion of a pre-employment physical exam, drug test, criminal background check, and motor vehicle records check is mandatory for employment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Final salary will be determined by the candidate’s experience, knowledge, and skills. Salary reflected does not include equity or variable pay, where applicable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salary Range: $22/hour&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is a 5 day/week onsite position. Flexible availability, including evenings, weekends, and holidays, is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There has never been a more exciting time to be on the cutting edge of public mobility. Ready to join the ride?&lt;/p&gt;
