&lt;p&gt;Via is on a mission to create public transportation systems that provide far greater access to jobs, healthcare, and education. Our platform serves as the technology backbone for modern transit networks, transforming antiquated and siloed public transportation systems into smart, data-driven, and efficient digital networks. With hundreds of agency partners around the world, Via is recognized as the leading transportation technology and service provider globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Engineering Manager, Mobile at Via, you’ll own a key product line and lead a team building mobile apps that power reliable, equitable and sustainable transit for communities worldwide. You’ll pair strategic leadership with end-to-end execution, shaping product direction, scaling core experiences, and driving meaningful real-world impact by building from the ground up on Via’s established platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the development of key mobile initiatives, such as improving rider/driver app performance, reliability, and user experience across iOS and Android&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and execute a roadmap focused on scalability (e.g. handling peak demand, optimizing app responsiveness, and reducing latency across core user flows)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive cross-functional projects with Product, Design, and Backend teams to launch new features end-to-end, from concept through production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve engineering quality and velocity by introducing better development practices, strengthening code review standards, and evolving mobile architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and grow a high-performing team by hiring, mentoring, and supporting engineers across different levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and lead improvements to team processes (e.g. release cycles, CI/CD, testing frameworks) to increase efficiency and reduce friction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to broader mobile initiatives, such as aligning on shared tooling, frameworks, and long-term platform strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience building mobile applications (iOS or Android), including experience working on production-scale apps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience leading engineering teams and delivering complex projects end-to-end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of mobile architecture, performance optimization, and modern development practices (e.g. CI/CD, testing, MVVM)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working across mobile, backend, and product domains to deliver cohesive solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative and pragmatic, able to balance speed with quality and make thoughtful trade-offs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on and detail-oriented when needed, while still operating effectively at a leadership level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communicator who builds trust across teams and creates a positive, inclusive team environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation and Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Final salary will be determined by the candidate’s experience, knowledge, and skills. Salary reflected does not include equity or variable pay, where applicable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salary Range: $215,000 - $265,000&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are proud to offer a generous and comprehensive benefits package, including free medical plans and 401K matching.&lt;/li&gt;
