&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This is an in-person position with the expectation that you will be onsite at least 3 days per week.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run daily onsite operations, ensuring safe, reliable, and accessible transportation for our riders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with a broad, cross-functional team to develop and scale the processes, systems, and tools that drive continuous optimization and support rapid growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make real-time decisions on fleet, driver supply, compliance, rider needs, and unexpected issues - using data to quickly diagnose problems and keep service running smoothly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide and support drivers, building strong relationships and coaching toward stronger performance in the field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn rider and community feedback into concrete changes by spotting patterns and addressing root causes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the bridge between Via’s partners, drivers, and Via central teams, keeping everyone informed with clear, timely updates and resolving questions quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operationally experienced in people management, logistics, customer service, or other process-oriented work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relationship-oriented and a confident communicator who builds trust with drivers, riders, teammates, and city partners, adapting their message and tone to each stakeholder, whether that’s partners, customers, or driver colleagues from diverse backgrounds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on and proactive, comfortable taking responsibility for employees, being in the field, and solving problems where they happen, even under pressure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytically savvy and structured, using data and digital tools to prioritize effectively and improve our services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tactical and strategic, able to tackle issues in real time while thinking ahead and building solutions that prevent them from recurring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid driver’s license in the UK, class B.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nice to have, but not required: Completed Certificate of Professional Competence (CPC) training and Qualified Transport Manager status would be a plus, as would experience in fixed-line bus operations.&lt;/li&gt;
