&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Via is a global leader in smart transportation, using technology to revolutionize mobility worldwide. Our impact ranges from transforming individual daily commutes to reducing the collective environmental cost of transit systems. We&#39;re driven by ambitious goals. This is an opportunity to join a core team reshaping how public mobility operates at scale.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Head of AI Research Product&lt;/strong&gt; to lead the intersection of applied machine learning research and product innovation across Via&#39;s rider and transit operations platform. This role sits at the frontier of what AI can do for public transportation, not as a feature layer, but as the engine that makes the system smarter, more equitable, and more efficient for every rider and agency we serve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a three-part role: innovating with lighthouse customers to pilot and pressure-test cutting-edge approaches in real-world transit environments, conducting original applied research, and driving productization of proven methods into Via&#39;s core platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and lead Via&#39;s AI research product function, defining the roadmap for how machine learning advances rider experience and transit network performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and deploy reinforcement learning systems that optimize routing, pooling efficiency, and real-time dispatching, balancing rider satisfaction against vehicle utilization and transit agency cost targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pioneer AlphaGo-style machine learning for transit: combine deep reinforcement learning, and tree search over high-fidelity simulations of real transit networks, training policy and value networks that discover dispatching, pooling, and network-design strategies beyond what hand-built heuristics or conventional optimization can reach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop weighted ensemble models and multi-objective optimization frameworks that surface the right tradeoffs between competing system goals: wait times, cost per ride, emissions, and equity of service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Invent personalization systems that adapt the rider mobile experience in real time, surfacing relevant trip options, proactive alerts, and dynamic pricing signals, in close partnership with the rider mobile product team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research and productize behavioral incentive models that increase ridership and shift demand to improve aggregation: surge smoothing mechanisms, loyalty structures, and gamified engagement grounded in behavioral economics and causal inference.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with lighthouse transit agencies to co-develop and validate novel AI approaches, turning field pilots into scalable platform features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish rigorous experimentation infrastructure (A/B testing, contextual bandits, offline policy evaluation) to measure the real-world impact of model changes on rider behavior and agency outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we are looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MS or PhD in a quantitative field: machine learning, operations research, statistics, applied mathematics, or a related discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep hands-on proficiency in ML: reinforcement learning, supervised and unsupervised methods, probabilistic modeling, and optimization. Experience with AlphaGo-style approaches (self-play, Monte Carlo tree search, policy/value networks) and with large-scale real-time inference systems is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine user empathy: you think as carefully about what a rider or agency dispatcher experiences as you do about model architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Very user-minded and clear-eyed about outcomes for users. You work closely with the mobile and SaaS product teams on experimentation, and you know how to find the balance between a delightful user experience and service KPIs such as efficiency and rider experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business sense and product instincts: you know how to translate a research finding into a shipped product and a shipped product into a business outcome.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with engineering teams to move models from research into production at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of working with external customers or partners to iterate on novel solutions in ambiguous, real-world conditions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating across research, product, and commercial contexts: you can present a model architecture to an ML engineer and a product strategy to a transit authority CEO.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for building technology that makes public transit work better for everyone, especially riders in underserved communities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation and Benefits:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Final salary will be determined by the candidate’s experience, knowledge, and skills. Salary reflected does not include equity or variable pay, where applicable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salary Range: $250,000 - $310,000 per year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive health coverage, with low-cost dental and vision plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A 401(k) with a generous company match and vesting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully paid parental leave for new parents, with extended leave options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional benefits (mental health, pet insurance, and other wellness perks)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;20 days of paid time off (PTO) annually&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Ready to join the ride?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Via is an equal opportunity employer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Via is using technology to transform transportation around the world. From changing a single person&#39;s daily commute to reducing humanity&#39;s collective environmental footprint — we&#39;ve got huge goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As &lt;strong&gt;Head of Risk &amp;amp; Insurance&lt;/strong&gt;, you will lead Via&#39;s insurance program, shaping its strategy, structure, and operations, as well as continuing to expand it as we take on new business lines.&amp;nbsp; Reporting to the COO, you&#39;ll be close to the integral parts of the business where risk shows up first.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own Via&#39;s insurance program end-to-end: assess our risk profile, identify the coverage we need, and put risk programs in place across the markets we operate in&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with senior leadership on risk strategy, including coverage decisions, alternative risk transfer (captives, self-insured retentions), and how risk and insurance figure into Via&#39;s broader operational and financial planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage brokerage and carrier relationships: run renewals, evaluate quotes, negotiate terms, and select partners who can grow with us globally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the systems and team to manage claims and litigation efficiently: define how incidents are reported; how reserves are set; and how we run a highly effective claims management process&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a risk management strategy that goes beyond insurance: partner with Legal, Finance, and other internal teams to identify and reduce loss exposure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the internal infrastructure: put policies, processes, dashboards, and reporting in place so the rest of the company has clear visibility into our risks&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stand up the analytics that tell us whether the program is working: monitor loss ratios, claim frequency and severity, cost per mile, and retention thresholds and use them to inform every renewal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, grow and develop Via’s risk team as the program scales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have built and run an insurance program before — ideally one with significant operational&amp;nbsp; exposure, and ideally at a company operating across multiple jurisdictions. You know what excellent looks like because you&#39;ve built it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have at least 10+ years of experience in risk management, insurance, or a closely adjacent function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At the same time, you’re excited to build. You thrive in ambiguity and are excited to help scale a function at a rapidly growing company&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You think commercially. Insurance is both a cost to be optimized and a risk management tool to be wielded. You understand both sides and can make trade-offs that hold up to scrutiny&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are analytical and data-driven. You leverage claims, litigation, and operational insights to identify trends, evaluate risk, and drive decisions that improve outcomes and reduce costs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are operationally minded. You know how to translate strategy into process, headcount, and tooling and how to do it in a way that scales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are hands-on and low ego — no task is too small if it helps contributes to Via’s success&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation and Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Final salary will be determined by the candidate&#39;s experience, knowledge, and skills. Salary reflected does not include equity or variable pay, where applicable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salary Range: $200,000 - $300,000 / year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are proud to offer a generous and comprehensive benefits package, including free medical plans and 401K matching.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ready to join the ride?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Via is an equal opportunity employer.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;At Citymapper (a Via company), we’re on a mission to help make complex cities more accessible to everyday users. Our application transports millions of people in hundreds of cities around the world by giving them access to the most current and sophisticated transportation options available&lt;strong&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As &lt;strong&gt;Head of Sales &lt;/strong&gt;at Via, you will scale &lt;a href=&quot;https://ads.citymapper.com/&quot;&gt;Citymapper&#39;s advertising business &lt;/a&gt;into a global force by deepening the company&#39;s presence in both direct and programmatic ecosystems across its core markets. This is a true player/coach role: you&#39;ll lead and grow a lean sales team while staying personally close to the most important deals, clients, and markets. It&#39;s a rare opportunity to operate with startup autonomy inside a company that moves millions of people every day, with real ownership over a business that&#39;s already found its footing and is ready for its next phase of growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end commercial strategy for Citymapper Ads across the UK, France, and the US: from identifying the highest-value prospects to closing and growing tier-one media buyer relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and deepen Citymapper&#39;s presence in both direct and programmatic buying ecosystems, including managing agency and brand partnerships, reseller networks, and SSP relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach, and grow a lean sales and account management team. You will set the bar for what great looks like, while staying personally close to the most complex deals and senior client relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Step in wherever the business needs you: whether that&#39;s troubleshooting a campaign, covering an account, or rolling up your sleeves on ad ops, you see no task as beneath your role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate market signals and customer feedback into actionable product insights, acting as the commercial voice in cross-functional conversations with product and engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and execute comprehensive sales strategies that identify new revenue opportunities, build direct relationships with agencies and brands, and consistently exceed targets across core markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in digital media sales or ad tech leadership, with deep fluency in both direct brand/agency sales and programmatic ecosystems (SSPs); French language skills are a strong plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established network across agency and brand contacts in the UK, US, and ideally France, with demonstrated success managing the full business development cycle from sourcing through close and consistently exceeding revenue targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable owning forecasting and commercial reporting, with a track record of translating pipeline data into accurate projections and clear strategic recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A genuine player/coach: you lead from the front, set high standards, and are equally comfortable running a high-stakes pitch and jumping into a campaign operations issue when the team needs it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A self-starter who thrives in fast-moving, ambiguous environments — highly organised, detail-oriented, and able to juggle multiple priorities without losing momentum or dropping the ball&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong communicator and collaborator who builds trust quickly across geographies, functions, and seniority levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Becoming part of a company that was awarded for its commitment to social good&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The chance to work alongside our award-winning ads team -nominated for multiple industry awards including DRUM, Campaign, and AOP, most recently winning the &lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ukaop.org/digital-publishing-awards/2026-winners&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;AOP Publishing Innovation Award&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; for our In-Journey Video Ads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation including equity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A hybrid working model and a spacious office near Chancery Lane, where you can enjoy weekly team lunches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive benefits package, including generous paid parental leave, and health scheme offered through AXA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partnership with YellowNest, a salary exchange benefit that helps reduce childcare fees for working parents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cycle to Work Scheme - multiple options via Green Commute Initiative (GCI)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There has never been a more exciting time to be on the cutting edge of public mobility. Ready to join the ride?&lt;/p&gt;
