&lt;p&gt;Via is on a mission to create public transportation systems that provide far greater access to jobs, healthcare, and education. Our platform serves as the technology backbone for modern transit networks, transforming antiquated and siloed public transportation systems into smart, data-driven, and efficient digital networks. With hundreds of agency partners around the world, Via is recognized as the leading transportation technology and service provider globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;As a &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Legal Operations Associate&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;, you will work closely with a team of highly dedicated and dynamic lawyers on a number of high impact topics like contracting, managing end-to-end processes, and other essential in-house legal functions. As a fully integrated member of the legal team, you will play a key cross functional role in driving success on a variety of exciting legal initiatives.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare, review and mark up contracts, e.g. NDAs, SaaS licenses, vendor contracts, engagement letters, etc., and maintain the company’s forms and guideline documents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research applicable federal, state and local laws, and regulations and ordinances, for a wide variety of domestic and international on-demand transit deployments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate regulatory requirements to operations teams and build processes to ensure regulatory compliance, especially with Department of Transportation and Federal Transit Administration regulations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop working knowledge of internal databases and systems in order to pull and extract insights from data in making business decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Constantly help the legal team become more organized and efficient, through the implementation and management of ticketing systems, document management and filing systems, KPIs tracking, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage, organize and maintain files in the company’s contract database and shared cloud storage system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure and track compliance with GDPR and other data privacy laws through oversight of Data Protection Agreements with vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure and track compliance with federal and state background check requirements consistent with regulatory requirements and contractual obligations.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide administrative support and assist with special projects, as assigned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement the company’s billing guidelines and coordinate with outside counsel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Go-getter with minimum of 0-2 years professional work (or work-study) experience (prior startup or legal experience is a plus).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s or graduate degree with a strong academic record - this is a non-attorney role, though college graduates interested in attending law school in the future are encouraged to apply.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meticulous and vigilant, with a keen attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing to wear multiple hats and work on projects of all types, big and small.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High-energy and enjoy working autonomously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical and critical thinking skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A positive can-do attitude, good judgment, and the ability to effectively manage competing priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational and communication skills and an eagerness to help others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;All final pay rates and levels will be determined by candidates experience, knowledge, skills, and abilities of the applicant, internal equity, and alignment with market data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salary Range: $70,000-$85,000.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive health coverage, with low-cost dental and vision plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A 401(k) with company match and vesting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully paid parental leave for new parents, with extended leave options.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional benefits (mental health, pet insurance, and other wellness perks).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
