&lt;p&gt;Via is using technology to transform transportation around the world. From changing a single person’s daily commute to reducing humanity’s collective environmental footprint — we’ve got huge goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Partnership Proposals Lead &lt;/strong&gt;at Via, you&#39;ll craft persuasive, exceptionally-written proposals that forge new partnerships with cities, transit agencies, and other public transit providers. Working with members of Via’s Strategy and executive leadership teams, you will develop a deep understanding of our customers&#39; needs and goals, become an expert in Via’s unique positioning as a technology partner, and own high-quality written proposals for transformative mobility services. Partnership Proposals Leads gain wide-ranging experience in Via&#39;s products and services; no specific experience in technology or public transit services is required.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hone your strategic thinking skills by coordinating with Via’s Partnerships, Expansion, and Finance teams to develop strategies for winning high-stakes, competitive procurements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Become an expert in Via’s technology and product offerings, absorbing complex, sometimes technical specifications and distilling information into clear, easily-digestible prose for both internal and external audiences.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write, review, and copy-edit comprehensive long-form narrative proposals for potential partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate compelling original content by ascertaining an audience’s needs and deploying your familiarity with Via’s technology and operational capabilities, transit norms, and the latest innovations from across the industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead competitive procurements from beginning to end -- through evaluation, creation of exceptional proposal content, review, and submission.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct rigorous research by analyzing news stories, new service announcements, scopes of work, city histories, and other forms of information and synthesizing findings into insightful commentary.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skillfully manage communications with potential partners over the phone and email.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support senior team members during interviews and launches with cities and transit agencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re meticulous and thoughtful. You can pay attention to every detail in a complex project while, at the same time, relating each of them to the big picture in a coherent way. You can see the forest &lt;em&gt;and&lt;/em&gt; the trees.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a minimum of 4 years of experience with a record of achievement in roles that require extensive and impeccable written communication. This could take many forms: graduate theses and dissertations, business proposals, policy memos, creative non-fiction, or journalism, to name a few. If you&#39;ve won awards for your writing, that&#39;s a plus!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re passionate about having an impact and are excited about advancing Via&#39;s mission to build more efficient, sustainable, and equitable transit systems. You’re excited about urban studies, environmental studies, accessibility, equity, and public governance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have exceptional judgment and strategic intuition. You know when to push and when to compromise when crafting a persuasive narrative.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re a collaborative, on-task project manager. You keep things moving through strong, clear communication and can manage multiple stakeholders across a single project.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re a reliable, motivated self-starter. You enjoy fast-paced environments, aren’t deterred by setbacks or pivots, and thrive in roles requiring a very high degree of responsibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re data-savvy and believe in evidence-based arguments. You excel at crafting compelling narratives using a wide range of quantitative and qualitative metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re an academic high-achiever, preferably in the humanities or social sciences where you practiced qualitative analysis and long-form writing (undergraduate degree required; advanced degree preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;All final pay rates will be determined by candidates experience, knowledge, skills, and abilities of the applicant, internal equity, and alignment with market data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salary Range: $115,000-$160,000&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive health coverage, with low-cost dental and vision plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A 401(k) with company match and vesting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully paid parental leave for new parents, with extended leave options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional benefits (mental health, pet insurance, and other wellness perks)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re Via, and we build technology that changes the way the world moves. We’re driven by a simple mission: to create modern and efficient public transportation systems that provide far greater access to jobs, healthcare, and education. With our best in class suite of products, we make transit thrive.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our teams of world-class engineers, data-scientists, product managers, operations specialists, marketers, transit experts and more bring cutting-edge AI-powered software and innovative technology-enabled operations to our partners across the globe. Founded in 2012, Via builds solutions to digitize, automate, and enable data-driven decision making for entire transportation networks; fixed-route buses, microtransit, paratransit, school buses, autonomous vehicles, and more.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re excited to be at the forefront of modernizing the future of transportation, are up for solving tough problems, and willing to become/already are a transit nerd, we are the place for you. Even if your past experience doesn’t align perfectly with every qualification in the job description for this role, we encourage you to apply. You may be just the right candidate for this or other opportunities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ready to join the ride?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Via is an equal opportunity employer.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Via is the global leader in transportation technology, powering modern, data-driven transit networks for hundreds of agency partners worldwide. Now, we are building our next frontier: AI Labs. This new, high-growth vertical combines Via’s global scale with cutting-edge artificial intelligence to build next-generation software for cities, automate complex systems, and unlock massive revenue opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Partnerships Associate&lt;/strong&gt;, you will operate at the intersection of marketing and sales to support the growth of AI Labs. You will own the research and outreach strategies to generate meaningful engagement with top prospects and customers, facilitating the partnerships that bring equitable and affordable transit to communities worldwide and supercharging the public sector with AI solutions.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an exciting role, tasked with building a book of business for a fast-growing new vertical. You’ll play a key role in shaping the team’s approach and helping cities develop new AI solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build pipeline for AI Labs, a new vertical dedicated to improving how cities function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform deep-dive research on accounts and individuals to create comprehensive buying committee maps and informed account plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead multi-channel outreach campaigns across email, phone, and LinkedIn to articulate the value of Via’s AI solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate meetings, provide demos, qualify leads, and close deals as appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and optimize sales tools within our CRM and marketing tech stack to ensure data accuracy and process scalability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with commercial teams to align outreach efforts with broader sales goals and regional growth strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 1–3 years of experience in B2B marketing, account-based marketing, or a sales development (BDR/SDR) role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical mindset with the ability to use campaign data to identify what’s working and where to pivot strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in CRM and marketing automation tools to manage high volumes of outreach and research effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, concise communicator capable of writing professional outreach and explaining complex AI solutions simply.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hungry to learn about AI, automation opportunities in the Public Sector, and the Via buying audience, with a proven ability to implement feedback quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resilient and team player who enjoys building relationships over time and remains undeterred by setbacks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation and Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;All final pay rates and levels will be determined by candidates experience, knowledge, skills, and abilities of the applicant, internal equity, and alignment with market data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salary Range: $70,000-$80,000 + $5k bonus target&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive health coverage, with low-cost dental and vision plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A 401(k) with company match and vesting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully paid parental leave for new parents, with extended leave options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional benefits (mental health, pet insurance, and other wellness perks)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There has never been a more exciting time to be on the cutting edge of public mobility. Ready to join the ride?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Via is an equal opportunity employer.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position:&lt;/strong&gt; Partnerships Associate Principal, Via Transportation, Inc. (New York City, NY) - &lt;em&gt;Telecommuting permitted&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Duties:&lt;/strong&gt; Conduct market research and analyze student transportation trends, customer needs, competitor offerings, and procurement patterns to support go-to-market recommendations for Via Student Transit. Conduct outreach interviews with school district, county, and nonprofit stakeholders to gather market intelligence and assess transportation needs, challenges, and purchasing considerations. Measure the effectiveness of outreach initiatives and recommend engagement approaches based on customer response data and market insights. Collect and analyze customer feedback and operational requirements from prospective educational organizations to evaluate product-market fit and inform marketing strategies. Analyze market conditions, competitive activity, and customer adoption trends and provide recommendations to improve product positioning and market competitiveness. Develop expertise in the student transportation market and analyze competitive offerings, customer needs, and industry trends to recommend positioning and differentiation strategies for Via Student Transit. Research customer preferences and market demand to develop data-driven messaging, positioning, and communication materials. Build targeted email outreach campaigns targeted at school districts and county departments to increase engagement and awareness amongst school districts and county departments. Analyze solicitation requirements, conduct market and customer research, and prepare Request for Proposal content tailored to organizational needs and procurement objectives. Develop Via Student Transit marketing materials, leveraging technical and emotional messaging. This includes building webinar content, writing blog posts/marketing handouts in collaboration with the Marketing team. Analyze marketing performance data and market research findings to develop recommendations regarding messaging, positioning, value proposition, and marketing initiatives. This involves data driven and story telling capabilities. Partner with internal teams to develop proposals, presentations, and communications materials that effectively communicate Via Student Transit’s capabilities and solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary:&lt;/strong&gt; $64,834 to $87,500&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements: &lt;/strong&gt;Bachelor’s Degree or higher (or foreign educational equivalent) in Marketing, Communications, or related field. Two years of experience in the offered position, or in a similar occupation, involving the development and use of business and sales analytics for strategic marketing planning and execution in the transportation or logistics industry. Experience utilizing Salesforce CRM or similar customer relationship management platforms. Telecommuting permitted.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contact: &lt;/strong&gt;Sharon Lee, SVP, People Operations&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Via Transportation, Inc.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;114 5th Avenue, 17th Floor&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;New York, NY, 20022&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;(888) 501-7511&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:strategic-growth-us@ridewithvia.com&quot;&gt;strategic-growth-us@ridewithvia.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Via is an equal opportunity employer.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Via is on a mission to create public transportation systems that provide far greater access to jobs, healthcare, and education. Our platform serves as the technology backbone for modern transit networks, transforming antiquated and siloed public transportation systems into smart, data-driven, and efficient digital networks. With hundreds of agency partners around the world, Via is recognized as the leading transportation technology and service provider globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Partner Success Manager&lt;/strong&gt;, you’ll be the face and voice of Via for our partners both internally and externally. In this dynamic role, you’ll be responsible for building genuine and durable customer relationships while converting those relationships into opportunities for long-term revenue growth. You will serve as our partners’ trusted advisor by providing strategic guidance on operational, go-to-market, and product-related issues. Simultaneously, you will be an internal advocate for partners with Via by championing for new products and capabilities to facilitate the expansion of each partner’s service size and scope.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a US East Coast role. We&#39;re ideally looking for candidates in Miami or Atlanta (remote, but are open to other East Coast locations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the success of advanced transportation systems in our partner’s cities, acting as the primary point of contact for executive city and agency leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a trusted advisor and consultant to our partners, helping to convert their ideas and community needs into revenue opportunities for Via&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build deep and trusting long-term relationships with partners by identifying partner pain points, providing solutions, and recognizing opportunities for service growth and revenue generation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze daily, weekly, and long-term service performance data to provide partners with actionable recommendations that improve their services’ quality, efficiency, and growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate multi-year and highly complex contract renewals and service expansions to increase year-on-year revenue from each partnership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have minimum of 4+ years of relevant work experience, including client facing experience,&amp;nbsp;including (but not limited to) consulting, consultative customer success, or success at a high growth company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Entrepreneurial relationship builder who remains calm and collected when faced with highly complex, politically sensitive situations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quantitatively-inclined and data savvy; you may not be a SQL expert, but you enjoy drawing quick, insightful conclusions from complex data sets, asking critical questions, and synthesizing raw numbers into simple, actionable recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A reliable, motivated self-starter with a growth mentality. You enjoy fast-paced environments, aren’t deterred by setbacks or pivots, and thrive in roles requiring a very high degree of responsibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An excellent team player; you’re a meaningful individual contributor, and a mentor to others on your team. You view successes as a team effort, and enjoy working with others&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation and Benefits:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Base Salary Range: $85,000 - $110,000. Total compensation also includes variable pay and equity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive health coverage, with low-cost dental and vision plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A 401(k) with company match and vesting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully paid parental leave for new parents, with extended leave options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional benefits (mental health, pet insurance, and other wellness perks)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;20 days of paid time off (PTO) annually&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ready to join the ride?&lt;/p&gt;
