&lt;li&gt;Launch new Via services, taking ownership of the People Operations workstreams required to ensure new operations are staffed, supported, and ready to begin service on time and at the highest possible quality, while contributing to the strategic decision-making and entrepreneurial approach required to establish Via operations in new markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage comprehensive People Operations launch project plans across multiple concurrent deployments, including key milestones, dependencies, risks, and timelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate critical workforce readiness activities — hiring and onboarding, payroll and benefits implementation, HR systems, employee documentation, policies, and compliance — collaborating closely with Operations, Expansion, Recruiting, Payroll, Benefits, Legal, IT, and local market teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a key People Operations partner to local operational leaders and employees throughout the launch process, identifying and resolving complex or time-sensitive issues that could impact workforce readiness or launch timelines, and supporting workforce transitions and employee and labor relations matters — including partnering with union representatives and internal Labor and Legal teams where applicable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide guidance following service launch to help stabilize new operations, address workforce and operational challenges, and support the transition into steady-state operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to improve and standardize Via’s launch processes, developing scalable tools, processes, and best practices that can be applied across future deployments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
