&lt;p&gt;Via is using technology to transform transportation around the world. From changing a single person’s daily commute to reducing humanity’s collective environmental footprint — we’ve got huge goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Product Support &amp;amp; Operations Specialist &lt;/strong&gt;at Via, you’ll be at the core of how our partners experience our technology. When cities and operators run into issues with the platform that powers their transit networks, you&#39;re who they turn to.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role blends partner-facing work with deep technical problem-solving. You&#39;ll bridge the gap between partners&#39; day-to-day realities and Via&#39;s Product and Engineering teams. It&#39;s a great opportunity for early-career professionals to build deep technical expertise, gain cross-functional exposure, and make a real impact from day one. You&#39;ll build a strong foundation that makes this an ideal starting point for many directions at Via.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get up to speed quickly through hands-on training and mentorship, becoming a true expert on Via&#39;s platform, tools, and industry context.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dive into technical issues, troubleshoot, and solve problems fast, giving partners the clarity they need to keep their networks running.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build close relationships with partners, understanding their day to day and pain points so you can advise them in ways that consistently improve deployment outcomes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross-functionally with Product, Engineering, Operations, and Partner Success to tackle challenges that span multiple functions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spot product and process improvements, acting as the bridge between partners and technical teams to shape prioritization and scalability decisions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1-2 years of work experience, including internships; we welcome recent graduates eager to grow in a fast-paced, mission-driven environment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curious and eager: You love digging into how things work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keen to build a career in tech, with an open mind about where you&#39;ll want to focus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meticulous and analytical, with a strong process orientation and the ability to manage multiple priorities simultaneously.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An entrepreneurial problem-solver who doesn&#39;t accept the status quo and is always looking for smarter solutions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A natural communicator who instinctively finds the right tone in every situation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;While not required, fluency in an additional language (Spanish, German, Arabic, French, Italian, Dutch, or Japanese) is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We don&#39;t expect you to check every box. If you&#39;re excited about our mission, learn quickly, take ownership, and enjoy working collaboratively, we&#39;d love to hear from you!&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Base Salary Range: $65,000-$75,000 per year plus variable pay and equity as part of a total compensation package. Final compensation will be determined by the candidate’s experience, knowledge, and skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive health coverage, with low-cost dental and vision plans.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A 401(k) with company match and vesting.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully paid parental leave for new parents, with extended leave options.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional benefits (mental health, pet insurance, and other wellness perks).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;20 days of paid time off (PTO) annually.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
