&lt;p&gt;As a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Platform Engineer &lt;/strong&gt;at Via, you’ll join our R&amp;amp;D center in TLV. You’ll be part of a team of developers and devops engineers, directly contributing to our product by using cutting-edge technologies. You’ll take a critical part in our mission to shape the future of transportation, affecting tens of thousands of riders daily worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Platform Group&lt;/strong&gt; is a cross-functional group dedicated to building and maintaining the robust foundation on which Via operates. This team is responsible for designing, implementing, and managing cloud infrastructure, Kubernetes clusters, CI/CD systems, and tools that empower our development and production environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With a focus on enhancing developer experience, operational efficiency, and reliability, the team drives initiatives that:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement scalable and secure cloud infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain Kubernetes clusters and related tools, ensuring high availability and performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage edge gateways, WAF solutions, and other critical infrastructure components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and enforce CI/CD standards to streamline development and delivery workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build tools and automation to enhance productivity across engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the reliability, security, and scalability of production infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define infrastructure standards for dev teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, implement and develop tools for controlling infrastructure of micro services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build CI/CD automation and templates with GitLab&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, maintain and operate AWS and Kubernetes infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain an in-depth understanding of the applications and architecture at Via&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work in contact with other teams across the company to ensure smooth and documented changes to all environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and resolve problems in mission-critical services, automating remediation procedures to prevent recurrences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring ideas to the table, take ownership over their project timelines and deliverables and help us scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BSc. Computer Science or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of professional experience in backend or full-stack development in a product development team. Object oriented programming programming experience is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years experience as Devops/SRE in a production environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years experience with containers, Kubernetes, Helm, Argo CD&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years experience with AWS or GCP/Azure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years experience with CICD - GitLab/Jenkins/Github actions/etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with networking, distributed systems, SQL and NoSQL databases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Unix/Linux operating systems internals and administration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in English language&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advantage - Experienced with declarative IaC tools like Terraform, Cloudformation or Pulumi&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to a collaborative environment infused with professionalism, integrity, passion, and accountability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation and Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our product impacts millions of users around the world&amp;nbsp; providing alternative transport solutions that are more: efficient and accessible, changing cities to make them greener.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation package which includes base salary and equity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health insurance with a discount for family members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid work and a lovely office situated in the heart of TLV, in Midtown, close to the light rail and train station.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Career development and growth opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other perks: Freefit and other sports lessons, 10bis/Cibus - you choose!, happy hours, team events, communities and many more benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2012, Via pioneered the TransitTech category by using new technologies to develop public mobility systems, optimizing networks of buses, shuttles, wheelchair accessible vehicles, school buses, autonomous vehicles, and electric vehicles around the globe.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Building the world&#39;s most efficient, equitable, and sustainable transportation network for all passengers, including those with limited mobility, those without smartphones, and unbanked populations — Via works with its partners to lower the costs of public transit while providing transportation options that rival the convenience of a personal car while reducing environmental impact.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At the intersection of transportation and technology, Via is a visionary market leader that combines software innovation with sophisticated service design and operational expertise to fundamentally improve the way the world moves, providing technology in 650 communities and more than 35 countries and counting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are dedicated to building a diverse, inclusive and authentic workplace. If you’re excited about this role but your past experience doesn’t align perfectly with every qualification in the job description, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right candidate for this or other roles. All backgrounds, identities, and voices are welcomed and celebrated at Via.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ready to join the ride?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Via is an equal opportunity employer.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Redesign the operating system for public transit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Via is a global leader in smart public transportation, using technology to change how the world moves. Our Transit Operations platform powers on-demand, paratransit, school bus, and fixed-line service for public agencies, reaching hundreds of thousands of riders every week. For many of them, public transit isn&#39;t a convenience. It&#39;s how they get to a job, a hospital, or a classroom.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Checklists are where public-sector software starts. They shouldn&#39;t be where it stops. The real test is whether a dispatcher can fix a missed pickup in seconds, or whether a rider with a disability can book a trip without a phone call. Our users span paratransit eligibility managers, call center agents, dispatchers, and agency leaders, plus the riders, caregivers, and students on the other end. Each one deserves a product that&#39;s insights-first, obvious to use, and delightful, especially the communities with the fewest alternatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is your chance to redesign a complex, mission-critical platform with usability and delight as the bar. You&#39;ll also drive how design itself can be AI-led, moving from static mockups to rapid prototypes to production-ready code, working side by side with engineers. This isn&#39;t AI for AI&#39;s sake. It&#39;s a way to democratize great design and ship better real-world outcomes for the people who rely on transit most.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Product org is investing in Design and is looking for multiple candidates with varying degree of experience - this is a fast and growing team!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the redesign of our dispatch and booking platform, unifying the experience across on-demand, paratransit, school bus, and fixed-line service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make every workflow insights-first, so data surfaces the right decision at the right moment instead of sitting in a report.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design for the full cast of people who make transit work: eligibility managers, call center agents, dispatchers, riders, caregivers, and students, each with journeys that feel purposeful and efficient.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design around rider eligibility, special conditions, and disability aids so every trip is dignified and easy, especially for riders with the fewest alternatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive how our design team works with AI, from synthesizing research and exploring concepts to building rapid prototypes and production-ready code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work in a forward-deployed way: spend time with agencies and engineers, test ideas against real operations, and ship alongside the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Run research and usability testing, and partner with analysts to turn data into design decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the details, from concept to pixel-perfect execution, and make tradeoffs explicit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evolve our design system deliberately as we scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with product, analytics, and engineering across the full project lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you Bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years in digital product design, with a portfolio showing concept-to-launch leadership on complex products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A systems-thinking mindset and experience designing dense, data-rich, high-stakes workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A point of view on how AI changes the design process, and the curiosity to keep pushing it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort prototyping beyond Figma and moving work toward production code (or a strong drive to learn).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A high bar for craft and strong Figma and prototyping skills. Motion and interaction design is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication and the ability to explain the &quot;why&quot; behind your decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership, independence, and pragmatism about timelines, scope, and technical constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empathy for riders who depend on public transit and a real interest in equitable mobility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A degree in Design, HCI, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation and Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Final salary will be determined by the candidate’s experience, knowledge, and skills. Salary reflected does not include equity or variable pay, where applicable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salary Range: $175,000-$230,000&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive health coverage, with low-cost dental and vision plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A 401(k) with a generous company match and vesting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully paid parental leave for new parents, with extended leave options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional benefits (mental health, pet insurance, and other wellness perks)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;20 days of paid time off (PTO) annually&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Via is on a mission to create public transportation systems that provide far greater access to jobs, healthcare, and education. Our platform serves as the technology backbone for modern transit networks, transforming antiquated and siloed public transportation systems into smart, data-driven, and efficient digital networks. With hundreds of agency partners around the world, Via is recognized as the leading transportation technology and service provider globally.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About this role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Remix is Via&#39;s premier transit planning and scheduling platform, trusted by agencies worldwide to design networks, model scenarios, and optimize service. We&#39;re looking for a Senior Product Manager to own the Remix platform itself — its usability, scalability, and flexibility — ensuring Remix remains the most powerful and intuitive tool available to transit professionals globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits at the center of everything Remix does. You will own the platform foundation that every module is built on, champion AI-led insights that help agencies design better service and measure real performance, and maintain the end-to-end view from planning through operations and back — ensuring data flows in ways that make each step smarter than the last. You are equally comfortable setting long-term platform direction and rolling up your sleeves to sharpen individual features and make each module best in class.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Remix platform roadmap — usability, scalability, flexibility, and the cross-cutting capabilities that every module depends on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and drive the vision for AI-led insights within Remix, enabling transit agencies to make data-informed decisions about service design, network performance, and operational efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold the end-to-end product view: from network planning through scheduling and live operations, and back into planning via performance data — ensuring the platform is a continuous feedback loop, not a collection of disconnected tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and prioritize vertical feature investments across Remix modules, with the rigor to make each one best in class rather than broadly adequate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Partner with engineering and design to raise the bar on platform usability — reducing friction for planners, schedulers, and analysts without sacrificing the depth power users depend on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with data science and engineering to define how AI and analytics capabilities are surfaced in the product — what insights matter, when they appear, and how they drive action&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage directly with customers to understand workflow pain points, validate priorities, and pressure-test the roadmap against real operational needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current on industry trends, competitive products, and emerging technology to ensure Remix leads rather than follows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 5+ years of product management experience, including ownership of platform or infrastructure-layer products used in complex enterprise workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a big-picture thinker who can articulate a multi-year platform vision while also making sharp, well-reasoned prioritization calls at the feature level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong instincts for usability and product quality — you notice when something is harder than it needs to be, and you know how to fix it without breaking what works&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You understand how AI and data products actually work in practice, and you have experience defining how analytical insights should be integrated into operational workflows in ways users trust and act on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can quickly become technically fluent in the underlying data models and entities that power planning and scheduling systems, and you are a credible voice in technical architecture decisions alongside your engineering partners — capable of evaluating tradeoffs and advocating for platform choices that serve both current needs and long-term scalability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a track record of shipping high-quality features in complex, workflow-heavy enterprise environments where precision and reliability matter&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are collaborative, direct, and effective at building alignment across engineering, design, data science, and go-to-market partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in transportation, transit, logistics, or resource-intensive industries is a plus; the ability to learn a technical domain quickly is essential&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation and Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Base salary range: $150,000-$220,000, determined by experience and skills. Total compensation also includes variable pay and equity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive health coverage, with low-cost dental and vision plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A 401(k) with a generous company match and vesting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully paid parental leave for new parents, with extended leave options.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional benefits (mental health, pet insurance, and other wellness perks).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;20 days of paid time off (PTO) annually.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
